{"title":"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Non-trig)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Non-trig)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(System_of_Equations)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (System of Equations)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5:\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5:</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are located on square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/7/22761b5d8de33620b8f3087e1e7a3e8e6b20dfe5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BEF$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is equilateral. What is the ratio of the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/872e3b09425c9659d782119a543dc858aa520a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> to that of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/9057d4d264f5530ac63d366089bc3c17ce5d79a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/c/0acdbd9175edadf6ebc85fa2b0eaaaeb9737e067.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(3 cm);  pair A, B, C, D, E, F;  A = (0,0); B = (1,0); C = (1,1); D = (0,1); E = (0,Tan(15)); F = (1 - Tan(15),1);  draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); draw(B--E--F--cycle);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, NW); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, W); label(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, N); [/asy]\" width=\"192\" height=\"185\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/7/bc743154094a7b78db1b49ee75537ad65700619c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } \\frac{4}{3} \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } \\frac{3}{2} \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } \\sqrt{3} \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } 2 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } 1+\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"412\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/4/4e4050342f16694c6946c030b5d594bdcf7aad34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BEF$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> is equilateral, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f375e35ba9dfc8e91ebf69ccb65d3bd2bd753999.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EA=FC$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e30e7dec97a3f5e84e0de8a12e3056c6c9a77fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EAB$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/a/3ca61b798add37d72a65243434f22b0f22cbb0b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FCB$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/d/c0db3c8193c12bef45baedaa46a1559d9d2b74c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HL$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> congruent. Thus, triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9e8b2c23e0545ef6de81f0ea578173e9ab7a64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is an isosceles right triangle. So we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7af0d224662e00a30f3826dc3c123c70d3e06630.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/2/c920b0f98f3d2b096ffd6483457b577e48047913.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF=EB=FB=x\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"194\" height=\"18\" />. If we go angle chasing, we find out that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/b/56b53162dfd91186e30d3d1425c8bf66d9b64647.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AEB=75^{\\circ}$\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" />, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/d/f2d9b006e36ee190e34dcffd0641970318d7e809.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABE=15^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/6/fd6a17d16a603e6863fb70dd1d48561558db16d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AE}{EB}=\\sin{15^{\\circ}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"206\" height=\"41\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/7/61798af32ae760bbdf7c37d394fafa673cf616e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AE}{x\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"136\" height=\"45\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/3/9036e960d3bc37278a4953f97634a775c42905ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=\\frac{x(\\sqrt{3}-1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"135\" height=\"41\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/1/e41ab8abd73e4878da24d42a9b38cf2b99055d2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=\\frac{x(\\sqrt{3}+1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"135\" height=\"41\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/9/b99b31202c9f900565728bf544d4b608bdd9e9cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABE]=\\frac{x^2}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"39\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b300a7a7522f8fe2d801c3ead97e23d8c9c55646.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[DEF]=\\frac{x^2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"98\" height=\"39\" />. Thus the ratio of the areas is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/0/b5075c652994213397aa0f1e00f91080a3308b8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"29\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Non-trig.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Non-trig)\">Solution 2 (Non-trig)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Non-trig)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>WLOG, let the side length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be 1. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/8/d6816609a18881fafb804083c7701e6107e0a685.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE = x$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" />. It suffices that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/d/2adbfa69041868dce5d01bae03b611c496381d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = 1 - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"93\" height=\"13\" />. Then triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd85454c0ce4000c0e63b4a1c4a12ef6f8b56e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/5/d454ccad55388ce38766e919a448421c4633323a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CBF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> are congruent by HL, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/4/a94c286b3e0cc2c721ed7e41cdf12f8c02e8d676.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF = AE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/9/0590eca5577acd7efc923db445dbc81fc46281fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE = DF$\" width=\"84\" height=\"12\" />. We find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/8/f88a3bad0f595be5c87c5be991c647ee5183546e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE = EF = x \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />, and so, by the Pythagorean Theorem, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d80ac117a840df1cfaa9981685d0c457da2519e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1 - x)^2 + 1 = 2x^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"19\" /> This yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/e/83e31cbee78c704dfafe631b1bee362b56a4168d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + 2x = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/b/bcb77ee671e353fd71f8527d0c1d4136bce544c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 = 2 - 2x$\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, the desired ratio of areas is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/b/1eb834d75f6292257508b55e9cce0086f3b3b973.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{\\dfrac{x^2}{2}}{\\dfrac{1-x}{2}} = \\dfrac{x^2}{1 - x} = \\boxed{\\text{(D) }2}.\\]\" width=\"197\" height=\"81\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28System_of_Equations.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(System_of_Equations)\">Solution 3 (System of Equations)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (System of Equations)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/4/4e4e71e9c0786b12fb9b4b5c67364147ed6e402f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/e/f1e715454d4a9ea7decd4afc39bb1630bdf82ad4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FC$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/2/bc2afec04e3636c80fa3d89e5468045595151c4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ED$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/8/b08aa5a28c62ed05af271aee7e5e053a0d4179b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />. We see that using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/d/c0db3c8193c12bef45baedaa46a1559d9d2b74c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HL$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/a/3ca61b798add37d72a65243434f22b0f22cbb0b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FCB$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> is congruent to EAB. Using Pythagoras of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/a/3ca61b798add37d72a65243434f22b0f22cbb0b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FCB$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/2/b72ff58bda9e7356fcecd58bdebc792f08d78c72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FDE$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/4/f84bdb345d33c0bd3e3088ea866042c918e00a8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2{(1-x)}^2=x^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"21\" />. Expanding, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/7/cc79daa7213ade202fcfd470772c89e54425206b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x^2-4x+2=x^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"172\" height=\"16\" />. Simplifying gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/a/20ae7dbafde8920e71ffec9c7f8a2b47f17e7f0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-4x+1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" /> solving using completing the square (or other methods) gives 2 answers: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/1/f41baaec7a97060dca470fab2660aef9bda8530e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2-\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/d/16d2c7ef186745cbfcaa694d1ea7749a2277a395.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/a/1faf5d41cd05857f8f0cbab1eb5a41bb1a6741f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/2/0b202b1703bf7352bc774c607836cce5c65c39b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2-\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />. Using the areas, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e5193f4044d319a612786bc133625da44ebc2d0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(D) }2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"53\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/9/319263bd6cc9471bb74d1b2036e83237b7419178.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup BEF$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is equilateral and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a square, by the Hypothenuse Leg Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/1/2816113f65ba2479f2b96ac29e5eb6ed0cdd6b31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup ABE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/6/236cf791c0c507bc096373a83f477b5666619f6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup CBF$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />. Then, assume length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/f/92f5587ea65df10eeca4919cc3c20be110444b08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = BC = x$\" width=\"116\" height=\"13\" /> and length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/c/1cc3b6311ed26a2e8f702407cab5a0d5d9c4d633.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE = DF = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"117\" height=\"16\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/6/52672569ac10536f23a2bb9ba671257bba65d5f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = FC = x - y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"146\" height=\"16\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/9/319263bd6cc9471bb74d1b2036e83237b7419178.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup BEF$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is equilateral, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/6/db6629625a8688eb10dcd519fea1c10b9334c529.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF = EB$\" width=\"81\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/3/793ff26c151189fb405a44c4938e6b42edb5481d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EB^2 = EF^2$\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" />, it is given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a square and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/c/9ec037942c70d50177f2c40554afd3d32fb096cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup DEF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/1/2816113f65ba2479f2b96ac29e5eb6ed0cdd6b31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup ABE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> are right triangles. Then we use the Pythagorean theorem to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/9/9a99ea0a3c5d10d5296b465cf981afcb41cabae8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB^2 + AE^2 = EB^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"153\" height=\"16\" /> and since we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/3/793ff26c151189fb405a44c4938e6b42edb5481d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EB^2 = EF^2$\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/d/eed82251ebca9f071e63e15ef39f1f3e1878c4e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF^2 = DE^2 + DF^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"156\" height=\"16\" />, which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/5/365eb8ad666d4606636e3b05b2a9d31b7f935977.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB^2 + AE^2 = DE^2 + DF^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"213\" height=\"16\" />. Now we plug in the variables and the equation becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/4/b54add0cd6ed6b0f75ef647f9a208eeb6c8c25c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + (x-y)^2 = 2y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"21\" />, expand and simplify and you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/4/8b42019f02f41cb2bafda2103f500e13b278d631.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x^2 - 2xy = y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" />. We want the ratio of area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/c/9ec037942c70d50177f2c40554afd3d32fb096cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup DEF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/1/2816113f65ba2479f2b96ac29e5eb6ed0cdd6b31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup ABE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />. Expressed in our variables, the ratio of the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/9/f8962d48b59db93aeb87249afbc2d7d34cbfce46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{y^2}{x^2 - xy}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"62\" height=\"42\" /> and we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/4/8b42019f02f41cb2bafda2103f500e13b278d631.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x^2 - 2xy = y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" />, so the ratio must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. So, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e5193f4044d319a612786bc133625da44ebc2d0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(D) }2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"53\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5:\">Solution 5:</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5:\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/4/4e4e71e9c0786b12fb9b4b5c67364147ed6e402f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/a/8fa77223787febae67680709fcf22abd9e65cdc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ED = DF = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"121\" height=\"14\" />. Then, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/5/3a57cd8acfbd55f55514ffb44ae8aec09b4e4304.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[DEF] = \\frac{x^2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"102\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/2/1825a8929028c0ab220508ad43a7524e578237b9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[ABE] = \\frac{(AE)(AB)}{2} = \\frac{(1-x)(1)}{2},\\]\" width=\"275\" height=\"38\" />so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/4/c246dbc3bf99ebb79a4e41be947e033055102d24.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{[DEF]}{[ABE]} = \\frac{x^2}{1-x} .\\]\" width=\"129\" height=\"44\" />By the Pythagorean Theorem applied to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/872e3b09425c9659d782119a543dc858aa520a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/8/48894e22d3faf1ca31fd744c2ab2f1faebaefd16.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[EF^2 = DE^2 + DF^2 = 2x^2.\\]\" width=\"211\" height=\"17\" />Applying the Pythagorean Theorem to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/b/a1b3b8188354494cb248bd9965a24d0b9f1ef814.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AEB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f002ab6b278d81722e9784d17bef9d823c100a8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[EB^2 = AB^2 + AE^2 = 1 + (1-x)^2 = 2 - 2x + x^2.\\]\" width=\"391\" height=\"20\" />Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae91ce43214ef7cd53d4ef57350933c86fa19909.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EFB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is equilateral, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/6/db6629625a8688eb10dcd519fea1c10b9334c529.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF = EB$\" width=\"81\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/f/70fb1eb543cf883d41ddc1eec5b333a155bc25f3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2x^2 = 2-2x + x^2,\\]\" width=\"145\" height=\"19\" />or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a3836f86bf11bb0eea705511055ec70221ab4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 = 2-2x= 2(1-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"184\" height=\"21\" />. Hence the desired ratio of the areas is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/b/44b125f5e84488e475bcd6028ec392c547916d74.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{[DEF]}{[ABE]} = \\frac{x^2}{1-x} = \\boxed{2}.\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"44\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let a side on the square be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and let the length of segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/92949d8236f0860c47eaf55c5c043eece2605b75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" />. Thus the ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/9/3691d90a13e2e718fbda07f1e61440ef985ae724.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\triangle [DEF]}{\\triangle [ABE]}=\\frac{(x-y)^2}{xy}=\\frac{x^2-2xy+y^2}{xy}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"305\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Also, if we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be a side of the equilateral triangle, by Pythagorean's theorem we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/d/38d6171ca1d5c023ba10f1f51d1682ea0437a89f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE^2 + DF^2 = 2(x-y)^2 = c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"235\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/f/1bf06428991417b693f20c2a8e88e43a326489b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE^2 + AB^2 = x^2 + y^2 = c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"216\" height=\"20\" />. Setting the equations equal to each other and rearranging yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/7/18770704db2f5821928f40086ffefe1f2743ac49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y^2=4xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>That expression can be substituted into our original equation:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/f/3ff49d43a9c06ab78ede312f7d78b03818f56fa8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x^2-2xy+y^2}{xy} = \\frac{4xy-2xy}{xy} = \\boxed{\\text{(D) }2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"298\" height=\"44\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/hwHIHRukYMk\">https://youtu.be/hwHIHRukYMk</a>\n</p><p>Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/BFKo9h8GhLY\">https://youtu.be/BFKo9h8GhLY</a> \n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A\">2004 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017112048\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.060 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.101 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 621/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18233/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.209      1 -total\n 60.57%    8.001      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 38.42%    5.075      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5567:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017112048 and revision id 291005. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}